  "id": "MAL-2026-20278",
  "summary": "Malicious code in promise-retry-utils-testmetest (npm)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (741b012db178dab26fc3deb78a568ad8137a096b5da56e399eca35599e567c00)\npackage.json for promise-retry-utils-testmetest@1.0.1 declares a `preinstall` lifecycle hook that executes `node setup.js` on `npm install`. The package name is a typosquat-shaped variant of the widely used promise-retry utility family and has no apparent legitimate purpose for a preinstall step. The script runs automatically on installation before any consumer code is invoked, so any behavior in setup.js — including environment or credential reads, outbound network, or payload execution — fires on default install.\n",
